From: georgii pl <gp@fx.gl>
Subject: [PATCH] venus: query KosmicKrisp external legacy tiling

KosmicKrisp's macOS renderer emulates dma-bufs through shared host imports,
not a native dma-buf tiling contract. Let its host external-image query decide
support and limits. steamac KK 0088 uses bounded linear backing for explicitly
shared host images, and virglrenderer 0020 preserves that external marker.

Keep the existing refusal for native dma-buf renderers. This is a local
steamac workaround for #58, not an upstream fix or a generic tiling override.

--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c
@@ -2798,8 +2798,11 @@
-      /* venus doesn't support legacy tiling for scanout purpose */
+      /* Native dma-buf scanout requires an explicit tiling contract.
+       * KosmicKrisp uses the macOS renderer's shm/host-import emulation;
+       * its external image query supplies the interoperable layout limits. */
       if (renderer_handle_type ==
              VK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HANDLE_TYPE_DMA_BUF_BIT_EXT &&
+          physical_dev->renderer_driver_id != VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_KOSMICKRISP &&
           pImageFormatInfo->tiling !=
              VK_IMAGE_TILING_DRM_FORMAT_MODIFIER_EXT) {
          return vn_error(physical_dev->instance,
                          VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED);
       }
